        "by": {
          "claim": "An attacker who compromises a low-privilege Application can reach the diff execution surface by triggering a comparison, gaining unbounded write authority across every resource kind in the cluster because the diff path executes as the cluster credential from the cluster Secret rather than honoring the destinationServiceAccounts least-privilege boundary. The Kubernetes API server authorizes the server-side apply dry-run as a real patch before evaluating the dry-run flag, and the check is enforced only in the sync execution context; the diff path lacks the destinationServiceAccounts resolution, leaving the cluster credential's broad permissions exposed.",
          "citations": [
            "rfc-001-sync-impersonation.md",
